        {
            "_id": "DMPZzJRT2zv3Zzfr",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Vitrification",
            "sort": 1500000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>This lerritan is so ancient that its molten core no longer burns as hot as it once did. At the end of each of its turns, it must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:48] save to avoid being @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Slowed], with a failed save increasing its condition by 1 (or by 2 on a critical failure) and a successful save reducing it by 1 (or by 2 on a critical success). If the lerritan becomes unable to act due to being slowed by vitrification, its movements grind to a halt as its body solidifies into an inanimate statue of volcanic glass, perhaps to stir anew in some far-distant future.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": []
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "JGXYh66auv2dCHDv",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Volcanic Eruption",
            "sort": 1600000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The volcano on the lerritan's back erupts and sends lava bombs raining down in a @Template[emanation|distance:30], dealing @Damage[12d12[fire]|options:area-damage] damage.</p>\n<p>Each creature in the area must attempt a @Check[reflex|dc:46|options:area-effect,damaging-effect,inflicts:encumbered,inflicts:immobilized] saving throw. The lava globules quickly cool into heavy stones, transforming the area into greater difficult terrain for non-lerritans.</p>\n<p>The lerritan can't use Volcanic Eruption for [[/gmr 1d4 #Recharge Volcanic Eruption]]{1d4 rounds}.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Encumbered] for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Immobilized] ([[/act escape dc=46]]).</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is encased in a rocky crust with lava on the inside. The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Restrained] ([[/act escape dc=46]]), can't breathe, takes @Damage[3d12[persistent,fire]] damage, and can't recover from this persistent fire damage until freed.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "earth",
                        "fire",
                        "primal"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        }
